0result.sql is more precise because it:

• Defines the “before” window (23‑Mar‑2020 → 14‑Jun‑2020) and the “after” window (15‑Jun‑2020 → 06‑Sep‑2020) so that each side contains exactly 12 weeks.  
• Filters the main data set to those dates only, guaranteeing no rows from a 13th week creep into the calculation.  
• Therefore its percentage‑change math reflects the requested 12‑week‑vs‑12‑week comparison, whereas 1result.sql extends the “after” period to 07‑Sep‑2020 (a 13th week), overstating “post” sales and skewing the result.

